#. type: TH
#: condinapt.1:3
#, no-wrap
msgid "CONDINAPT"
msgstr "CONDINAPT"

#. type: TH
#: condinapt.1:3
#, no-wrap
msgid "Conditional APT Package Installer"
msgstr "Installateur conditionnel de paquets APT"

#. type: Plain text
#: condinapt.1:7
msgid ""
"condinapt - plan and install APT packages from a conditional package list"
msgstr ""
"condinapt - planifier et installer des paquets APT à partir d'une liste "
"conditionnelle de paquets"

#. type: Plain text
#: condinapt.1:10
msgid ""
"\\f[B]condinapt\\f[R] \\f[B]-l\\f[R] \\f[I]PACKAGE-LIST\\f[R] \\f[B]-c\\f[R] "
"\\f[I]CONFIG\\f[R] [\\f[I]OPTIONS\\f[R]]\\fR"
msgstr ""
"\\f[B]condinapt\\f[R] \\f[B]-l\\f[R] \\f[I]PACKAGE-LIST\\f[R] \\f[B]-c\\f[R] "
"\\f[I]CONFIG\\f[R] [\\f[I]OPTIONS\\f[R]]\\fR"

#. type: Plain text
#: condinapt.1:17
msgid ""
"\\f[B]condinapt\\f[R] reads a Bash configuration and a package list, "
"evaluates package filters, checks package availability, groups selected "
"packages into APT transactions, and installs them.  It supports exact or "
"fallback versions, target releases, alternatives, conjunctions, mandatory "
"alternatives, queue separators, and a priority list.\\fR"
msgstr ""
"\\f[B]condinapt\\f[R] lit une configuration Bash et une liste de paquets, "
"évalue les filtres de paquets, vérifie la disponibilité des paquets, "
"regroupe les paquets sélectionnés en transactions APT, puis les installe. Il "
"prend en charge les versions exactes ou de repli, les versions de "
"distribution cibles, les alternatives, les conjonctions, les alternatives "
"obligatoires, les séparateurs de files d'attente et une liste de priorités."
"\\fR"

#. type: Plain text
#: condinapt.1:21
msgid ""
"The configuration file is sourced as Bash and must be trusted.  Package "
"installation and any APT list refresh normally require suitable privileges."
msgstr ""
"Le fichier de configuration est inclus comme du Bash et doit être digne de "
"confiance. L'installation de paquets et tout rafraîchissement des listes APT "
"nécessitent normalement les privilèges appropriés."

#. type: TP
#: condinapt.1:22
#, no-wrap
msgid "\\f[B]-l\\f[R], \\f[B]--package-list\\f[R] \\f[I]PATH\\fR"
msgstr "\\f[B]-l\\f[R], \\f[B]--package-list\\f[R] \\f[I]PATH\\fR"

#. type: Plain text
#: condinapt.1:25
msgid "Required package list."
msgstr "Liste de paquets requise."

#. type: TP
#: condinapt.1:25
#, no-wrap
msgid "\\f[B]-c\\f[R], \\f[B]--config\\f[R] \\f[I]PATH\\fR"
msgstr "\\f[B]-c\\f[R], \\f[B]--config\\f[R] \\f[I]PATH\\fR"

#. type: Plain text
#: condinapt.1:28
msgid "Required Bash configuration file containing filter variables."
msgstr ""
"Fichier de configuration Bash requis contenant les variables de filtrage."

#. type: TP
#: condinapt.1:28
#, no-wrap
msgid "\\f[B]-m\\f[R], \\f[B]--filter-mapping\\f[R] \\f[I]PATH\\fR"
msgstr "\\f[B]-m\\f[R], \\f[B]--filter-mapping\\f[R] \\f[I]PATH\\fR"

#. type: Plain text
#: condinapt.1:32
msgid ""
"Optional prefix-to-variable mapping.  Without it, filter prefixes are "
"interpreted directly as variable names."
msgstr ""
"Association optionnelle préfixe-vers-variable. Sans cela, les préfixes de "
"filtre sont interprétés directement comme noms de variables."

#. type: TP
#: condinapt.1:32
#, no-wrap
msgid "\\f[B]-P\\f[R], \\f[B]--priority-list\\f[R] \\f[I]PATH\\fR"
msgstr "\\f[B]-P\\f[R], \\f[B]--priority-list\\f[R] \\f[I]PATH\\fR"

#. type: Plain text
#: condinapt.1:38
msgid ""
"Optional file containing one Bash regular expression per line.  Expressions "
"match the first package token on each package-list line.  Matching lines are "
"moved to priority queues with their filters and target releases preserved."
msgstr ""
"Fichier optionnel contenant une expression rationnelle Bash par ligne. Les "
"expressions correspondent au premier jeton de paquet sur chaque ligne de la "
"liste de paquets. Les lignes correspondantes sont déplacées dans les files "
"de priorité, avec leurs filtres et versions de distribution cibles préservés."

#. type: TP
#: condinapt.1:38
#, no-wrap
msgid "\\f[B]-C\\f[R], \\f[B]--check-only\\fR"
msgstr "\\f[B]-C\\f[R], \\f[B]--check-only\\fR"

#. type: Plain text
#: condinapt.1:48
msgid ""
"Evaluate filters and report relevant package names that are not installed.  "
"Return 1 and print a suggested \\f[B]apt install\\f[R] command when packages "
"are missing.  This mode checks package names only; it does not validate "
"requested versions or target releases.  An alternative expression is "
"satisfied when one branch is installed; if none is installed, every failed "
"branch may be reported and suggested.\\fR"
msgstr ""
"Évalue les filtres et signale les noms de paquets pertinents qui ne sont pas "
"installés. Retourne 1 et affiche une commande \\f[B]apt install\\f[R] "
"suggérée lorsque des paquets sont manquants. Ce mode vérifie uniquement les "
"noms de paquets ; il ne valide pas les versions demandées ni les versions de "
"distribution cibles. Une expression alternative est satisfaite lorsqu'une "
"branche est installée ; si aucune ne l'est, chaque branche échouée peut être "
"signalée et suggérée.\\fR"

#. type: TP
#: condinapt.1:48
#, no-wrap
msgid "\\f[B]-s\\f[R], \\f[B]--simulation\\fR"
msgstr "\\f[B]-s\\f[R], \\f[B]--simulation\\fR"

#. type: Plain text
#: condinapt.1:54
msgid ""
"Plan the installation without installing packages.  Simulation always exits "
"with status 1.  It may still run \\f[B]apt-get update\\f[R] when the package "
"cache is absent or \\f[B]--force\\f[R] is used.\\fR"
msgstr ""
"Planifie l'installation sans installer les paquets. La simulation retourne "
"toujours le statut 1. Elle peut tout de même exécuter \\f[B]apt-get "
"update\\f[R] si le cache des paquets est absent ou si \\f[B]--force\\f[R] "
"est utilisé.\\fR"

#. type: TP
#: condinapt.1:54
#, no-wrap
msgid "\\f[B]-f\\f[R], \\f[B]--force\\fR"
msgstr "\\f[B]-f\\f[R], \\f[B]--force\\fR"

#. type: Plain text
#: condinapt.1:59
msgid ""
"Run \\f[B]apt-get update\\f[R] before normal installation or simulation even "
"when \\f[B]/var/cache/apt/pkgcache.bin\\f[R] exists.  It has no effect in "
"check-only mode.\\fR"
msgstr ""
"Exécute \\f[B]apt-get update\\f[R] avant l'installation normale ou la "
"simulation, même si \\f[B]/var/cache/apt/pkgcache.bin\\f[R] existe. Sans "
"effet en mode vérification uniquement.\\fR"

#. type: TP
#: condinapt.1:59
#, no-wrap
msgid "\\f[B]-v\\f[R], \\f[B]--verbose\\fR"
msgstr "\\f[B]-v\\f[R], \\f[B]--verbose\\fR"

#. type: Plain text
#: condinapt.1:62
msgid "Show filter decisions and direct APT output."
msgstr "Affiche les décisions de filtrage et la sortie directe d'APT."

#. type: TP
#: condinapt.1:62
#, no-wrap
msgid "\\f[B]-vv\\f[R], \\f[B]--very-verbose\\fR"
msgstr "\\f[B]-vv\\f[R], \\f[B]--very-verbose\\fR"

#. type: Plain text
#: condinapt.1:65
msgid "Show additional planning and priority-queue details."
msgstr ""
"Affiche des détails supplémentaires sur la planification et les files de "
"priorité."

#. type: TP
#: condinapt.1:65
#, no-wrap
msgid "\\f[B]-x\\f[R], \\f[B]--xtrace\\fR"
msgstr "\\f[B]-x\\f[R], \\f[B]--xtrace\\fR"

#. type: Plain text
#: condinapt.1:68
msgid "Enable Bash command tracing."
msgstr "Active le traçage des commandes Bash."

#. type: TP
#: condinapt.1:68
#, no-wrap
msgid "\\f[B]-h\\f[R], \\f[B]--help\\fR"
msgstr "\\f[B]-h\\f[R], \\f[B]--help\\fR"

#. type: Plain text
#: condinapt.1:71
msgid "Display help and exit."
msgstr "Affiche l'aide et quitte."

#. type: SH
#: condinapt.1:71
#, no-wrap
msgid "INPUT FILES"
msgstr "FICHIERS D'ENTRÉE"

#. type: SS
#: condinapt.1:72
#, no-wrap
msgid "Configuration"
msgstr "Configuration"

#. type: Plain text
#: condinapt.1:76
msgid ""
"The required configuration is a Bash file.  Scalar values compare by exact "
"string equality.  Indexed Bash arrays match when any element equals the "
"requested value."
msgstr ""
"La configuration requise est un fichier Bash. Les valeurs scalaires sont "
"comparées par égalité exacte de chaîne. Les tableaux Bash indexés "
"correspondent si un élément est égal à la valeur demandée."

#. type: Plain text
#: condinapt.1:82
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"DISTRIBUTION=\\[dq]bookworm\\[dq]\n"
"SYSTEM_TYPE=\\[dq]server\\[dq]\n"
"ENVIRONMENT=\\[dq]production\\[dq]\n"
"FEATURES=(web database)\n"
msgstr ""
"DISTRIBUTION=\\[dq]bookworm\\[dq]\n"
"SYSTEM_TYPE=\\[dq]server\\[dq]\n"
"ENVIRONMENT=\\[dq]production\\[dq]\n"
"FEATURES=(web database)\n"

#. type: SS
#: condinapt.1:83
#, no-wrap
msgid "Filter Mapping"
msgstr "Mappage des filtres"

#. type: Plain text
#: condinapt.1:86
msgid ""
"An optional mapping assigns short package-list prefixes to configuration "
"variables:"
msgstr ""
"Une association optionnelle attribue des préfixes courts de liste de paquets "
"à des variables de configuration :"

#. type: Plain text
#: condinapt.1:92
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"d=DISTRIBUTION\n"
"st=SYSTEM_TYPE\n"
"env=ENVIRONMENT\n"
"feat=FEATURES\n"
msgstr ""
"d=DISTRIBUTION\n"
"st=SYSTEM_TYPE\n"
"env=ENVIRONMENT\n"
"feat=FEATURES\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: condinapt.1:97
msgid ""
"An unmapped prefix is used as the variable name.  Missing variables have an "
"empty value.  Variable names must be valid Bash identifiers."
msgstr ""
"Un préfixe non associé est utilisé comme nom de variable. Les variables "
"manquantes ont une valeur vide. Les noms de variables doivent être des "
"identifiants Bash valides."

#. type: SS
#: condinapt.1:97
#, no-wrap
msgid "Package List"
msgstr "Liste de paquets"

#. type: Plain text
#: condinapt.1:100
msgid ""
"Each non-empty, non-comment line contains a package expression.  Text after "
"\\f[B]#\\f[R] is ignored.\\fR"
msgstr ""
"Chaque ligne non vide et non commentée contient une expression de paquet. Le "
"texte après \\f[B]#\\f[R] est ignoré.\\fR"

#. type: Plain text
#: condinapt.1:105
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"vim\n"
"nginx +st=server\n"
"debug-tools -env=production\n"
msgstr ""
"vim\n"
"nginx +st=server\n"
"debug-tools -env=production\n"

#. type: SS
#: condinapt.1:106
#, no-wrap
msgid "Priority List"
msgstr "Liste de priorités"

#. type: Plain text
#: condinapt.1:110
msgid ""
"Each non-empty, non-comment line is a Bash \\f[B]=\\[ti]\\f[R] regular "
"expression matched against the first package token in a package expression:"
"\\fR"
msgstr ""
"Chaque ligne non vide et non commentée est une expression rationnelle Bash "
"\\f[B]=\\[ti]\\f[R] appliquée au premier jeton de paquet d'une expression de "
"paquet :\\fR"

#. type: Plain text
#: condinapt.1:115
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\\[ha]linux-.*\n"
"\\[ha]firmware-.*\n"
"\\[ha]dkms$\n"
msgstr ""
"\\[ha]linux-.*\n"
"\\[ha]firmware-.*\n"
"\\[ha]dkms$\n"

#. type: SH
#: condinapt.1:116
#, no-wrap
msgid "PACKAGE SYNTAX"
msgstr "SYNTAXE DES PAQUETS"

#. type: SS
#: condinapt.1:117
#, no-wrap
msgid "Versions"
msgstr "Versions"

#. type: TP
#: condinapt.1:118
#, no-wrap
msgid "\\f[B]package=version\\fR"
msgstr "\\f[B]package=version\\fR"

#. type: Plain text
#: condinapt.1:123
msgid ""
"Request an exact version.  If it is unavailable but another candidate "
"exists, install the candidate and emit a warning."
msgstr ""
"Demande une version exacte. Si elle n'est pas disponible mais qu'un autre "
"candidat existe, installe le candidat et émet un avertissement."

#. type: TP
#: condinapt.1:123
#, no-wrap
msgid "\\f[B]package==version\\fR"
msgstr "\\f[B]package==version\\fR"

#. type: Plain text
#: condinapt.1:127
msgid ""
"Require an exact version during planning.  If it is unavailable, this "
"expression cannot be selected."
msgstr ""
"Exige une version exacte lors de la planification. Si elle n'est pas "
"disponible, cette expression ne peut pas être sélectionnée."

#. type: Plain text
#: condinapt.1:130
msgid ""
"When an exact requested version is selected and installed, "
"\\f[B]condinapt\\f[R] applies \\f[B]apt-mark hold\\f[R] to that package.\\fR"
msgstr ""
"Lorsqu'une version exacte demandée est sélectionnée et installée, "
"\\f[B]condinapt\\f[R] applique \\f[B]apt-mark hold\\f[R] à ce paquet.\\fR"

#. type: SS
#: condinapt.1:130
#, no-wrap
msgid "Target Releases"
msgstr "Versions de distribution cibles"

#. type: Plain text
#: condinapt.1:133
msgid ""
"Append \\f[B]\\[at]release\\f[R] to install through \\f[B]apt-get -t "
"release\\f[R]:\\fR"
msgstr ""
"Ajoute \\f[B]\\[at]release\\f[R] pour installer via \\f[B]apt-get -t "
"release\\f[R] :\\fR"

#. type: Plain text
#: condinapt.1:136
#, no-wrap
msgid "linux-image-amd64 \\[at]bookworm-backports\n"
msgstr "linux-image-amd64 \\[at]bookworm-backports\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: condinapt.1:141
msgid ""
"Entries for the same release are pooled into one release-specific queue.  "
"The \\f[B]\\[em]\\f[R] separator does not split target-release queues.\\fR"
msgstr ""
"Les entrées pour la même version de distribution sont regroupées dans une "
"file spécifique à cette version. Le séparateur \\f[B]\\[em]\\f[R] ne divise "
"pas les files de versions de distribution cibles.\\fR"

#. type: SS
#: condinapt.1:141
#, no-wrap
msgid "Filters"
msgstr "Filtres"

#. type: TP
#: condinapt.1:142
#, no-wrap
msgid "\\f[B]+prefix=value\\fR"
msgstr "\\f[B]+préfixe=valeur\\fR"

#. type: Plain text
#: condinapt.1:146
msgid ""
"Include the package when the mapped scalar equals \\f[I]value\\f[R] or an "
"array contains it.\\fR"
msgstr ""
"Inclure le paquet lorsque le scalaire mappé est égal à \\f[I]valeur\\f[R] ou "
"qu'un tableau le contient.\\fR"

#. type: TP
#: condinapt.1:146
#, no-wrap
msgid "\\f[B]-prefix=value\\fR"
msgstr "\\f[B]-préfixe=valeur\\fR"

#. type: Plain text
#: condinapt.1:150
msgid ""
"Exclude the package when the mapped scalar equals \\f[I]value\\f[R] or an "
"array contains it.\\fR"
msgstr ""
"Exclure le paquet lorsque le scalaire mappé est égal à \\f[I]valeur\\f[R] ou "
"qu'un tableau le contient.\\fR"

#. type: Plain text
#: condinapt.1:154
msgid ""
"Repeated positive filters with the same prefix are alternatives.  Positive "
"filters with different prefixes must each have at least one match:"
msgstr ""
"Les filtres positifs répétés avec le même préfixe sont considérés comme des "
"alternatives. Les filtres positifs avec des préfixes différents doivent "
"chacun avoir au moins une correspondance :"

#. type: Plain text
#: condinapt.1:157
#, no-wrap
msgid "editor +d=bookworm +d=trixie +st=desktop\n"
msgstr "editor +d=bookworm +d=trixie +st=desktop\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: condinapt.1:161
msgid ""
"The example selects Debian Bookworm or Trixie and also requires "
"\\f[B]SYSTEM_TYPE=desktop\\f[R].\\fR"
msgstr ""
"L'exemple sélectionne Debian Bookworm ou Trixie et exige également "
"\\f[B]SYSTEM_TYPE=desktop\\fR.\\fR"

#. type: Plain text
#: condinapt.1:163
msgid "Group filters make the relationship explicit:"
msgstr "Les filtres de groupe rendent la relation explicite :"

#. type: TP
#: condinapt.1:163
#, no-wrap
msgid "\\f[B]+{a|b}\\fR"
msgstr "\\f[B]+{a|b}\\fR"

#. type: Plain text
#: condinapt.1:166
msgid "Include when at least one condition matches."
msgstr "Inclure si au moins une condition correspond."

#. type: TP
#: condinapt.1:166
#, no-wrap
msgid "\\f[B]+{a&b}\\fR"
msgstr "\\f[B]+{a&b}\\fR"

#. type: Plain text
#: condinapt.1:169
msgid "Include only when every condition matches."
msgstr "Inclure uniquement si toutes les conditions sont remplies."

#. type: TP
#: condinapt.1:169
#, no-wrap
msgid "\\f[B]-{a|b}\\fR"
msgstr "\\f[B]-{a|b}\\fR"

#. type: Plain text
#: condinapt.1:172
msgid "Exclude when at least one condition matches."
msgstr "Exclure si au moins une condition correspond."

#. type: TP
#: condinapt.1:172
#, no-wrap
msgid "\\f[B]-{a&b}\\fR"
msgstr "\\f[B]-{a&b}\\fR"

#. type: Plain text
#: condinapt.1:175
msgid "Exclude only when every condition matches."
msgstr "Exclure uniquement si toutes les conditions sont remplies."

#. type: Plain text
#: condinapt.1:177
msgid "Examples:"
msgstr "Exemples :"

#. type: Plain text
#: condinapt.1:182
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"web-server +{st=server|st=web-server}\n"
"database-tools +{d=bookworm&st=server}\n"
"debug-tools -{env=production|st=minimal}\n"
msgstr ""
"web-server +{st=server|st=web-server}\n"
"database-tools +{d=bookworm&st=server}\n"
"debug-tools -{env=production|st=minimal}\n"

#. type: SS
#: condinapt.1:183
#, no-wrap
msgid "Alternatives And Conjunctions"
msgstr "Alternatives et Conjonctions"

#. type: TP
#: condinapt.1:184
#, no-wrap
msgid "\\f[B]left || right\\fR"
msgstr "\\f[B]gauche || droite\\fR"

#. type: Plain text
#: condinapt.1:190
msgid ""
"During planning, select the first alternative whose filters pass and whose "
"required packages are installed or available from APT.  It is not a runtime "
"fallback: if the later \\f[B]apt-get install\\f[R] transaction fails, "
"another alternative is not tried.\\fR"
msgstr ""
"Lors de la planification, la première alternative dont les filtres passent "
"et dont les paquets requis sont installés ou disponibles via APT est "
"sélectionnée. Il ne s'agit pas d'un repli à l'exécution : si la transaction "
"\\f[B]apt-get install\\fR échoue, aucune autre alternative n'est essayée.\\fR"

#. type: TP
#: condinapt.1:190
#, no-wrap
msgid "\\f[B]left && right\\fR"
msgstr "\\f[B]gauche && droite\\fR"

#. type: Plain text
#: condinapt.1:194
msgid ""
"Require every expression in the alternative to pass filtering and "
"availability checks before adding them to the same installation plan."
msgstr ""
"Chaque expression de l'alternative doit satisfaire les filtres et les "
"vérifications de disponibilité avant d'être ajoutée au même plan "
"d'installation."

#. type: Plain text
#: condinapt.1:196
msgid "\\f[B]&&\\f[R] binds within each \\f[B]||\\f[R] alternative:\\fR"
msgstr ""
"\\f[B]&&\\fR s'applique à l'intérieur de chaque alternative \\f[B]||\\fR :"
"\\fR"

#. type: Plain text
#: condinapt.1:199 condinapt-minios.7:201
#, no-wrap
msgid "exfatprogs || exfat-utils && exfat-fuse\n"
msgstr "exfatprogs || exfat-utils && exfat-fuse\n"

#. type: SS
#: condinapt.1:200
#, no-wrap
msgid "Mandatory Alternatives"
msgstr "Alternatives obligatoires"

#. type: Plain text
#: condinapt.1:202
msgid ""
"A leading \\f[B]!\\f[R] marks the entire package expression as mandatory:\\fR"
msgstr ""
"Un \\f[B]!\\fR en début de ligne marque toute l'expression de paquet comme "
"obligatoire :\\fR"

#. type: Plain text
#: condinapt.1:206
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"!essential-package\n"
"!preferred-package || fallback-package\n"
msgstr ""
"!essential-package\n"
"!preferred-package || fallback-package\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: condinapt.1:213
msgid ""
"If no alternative can be selected because required packages are unavailable, "
"normal execution aborts.  A valid later alternative satisfies the mandatory "
"expression.  Filter-only exclusions do not trigger a mandatory-package "
"abort, and simulation reports the failure without aborting early."
msgstr ""
"Si aucune alternative ne peut être sélectionnée parce que les paquets requis "
"sont indisponibles, l'exécution normale s'arrête. Une alternative valide "
"ultérieure satisfait l'expression obligatoire. Les exclusions par filtre "
"uniquement ne déclenchent pas d'arrêt pour paquet obligatoire, et la "
"simulation signale l'échec sans interrompre prématurément."

#. type: SH
#: condinapt.1:213
#, no-wrap
msgid "QUEUES"
msgstr "FILES D'ATTENTE"

#. type: Plain text
#: condinapt.1:218
msgid ""
"A line containing only \\f[B]\\[em]\\f[R] closes the current normal-"
"repository queue.  Packages in one queue are installed in a single APT "
"transaction, and normal queues run sequentially.\\fR"
msgstr ""
"Une ligne contenant uniquement \\f[B]\\[em]\\fR ferme la file d'attente du "
"dépôt normal en cours. Les paquets d'une même file sont installés lors d'une "
"seule transaction APT, et les files normales sont exécutées séquentiellement."
"\\fR"

#. type: Plain text
#: condinapt.1:221
msgid ""
"Target-release entries are pooled separately by release.  Processing order "
"is:"
msgstr ""
"Les entrées target-release sont regroupées séparément par version. L'ordre "
"de traitement est :"

#. type: IP
#: condinapt.1:221
#, no-wrap
msgid "1."
msgstr "1."

#. type: Plain text
#: condinapt.1:223
msgid "Priority normal-repository queue"
msgstr "File d'attente prioritaire du dépôt normal"

#. type: IP
#: condinapt.1:223
#, no-wrap
msgid "2."
msgstr "2."

#. type: Plain text
#: condinapt.1:225
msgid "Priority target-release queues"
msgstr "Files d'attente prioritaires target-release"

#. type: IP
#: condinapt.1:225
#, no-wrap
msgid "3."
msgstr "3."

#. type: Plain text
#: condinapt.1:227
msgid "Normal queues"
msgstr "Files normales"

#. type: IP
#: condinapt.1:227
#, no-wrap
msgid "4."
msgstr "4."

#. type: Plain text
#: condinapt.1:229
msgid "Remaining target-release queues"
msgstr "Files d'attente target-release restantes"

#. type: Plain text
#: condinapt.1:236
msgid ""
"The priority list removes matching expressions from their original queues "
"and preserves their complete filters, conditions, versions, and target "
"release.  Only the first package token is used for priority matching, so a "
"pattern that matches only a later \\f[B]||\\f[R] branch does not prioritize "
"the expression.\\fR"
msgstr ""
"La liste de priorité retire les expressions correspondantes de leurs files "
"d'origine et conserve l'intégralité de leurs filtres, conditions, versions "
"et version cible. Seul le premier jeton de paquet est utilisé pour la "
"correspondance de priorité, donc un motif qui ne correspond qu'à une branche "
"\\f[B]||\\fR ultérieure ne priorise pas l'expression.\\fR"

#. type: SH
#: condinapt.1:236
#, no-wrap
msgid "OPERATING MODES"
msgstr "MODES DE FONCTIONNEMENT"

#. type: SS
#: condinapt.1:237
#, no-wrap
msgid "Simulation"
msgstr "Simulation"

#. type: Plain text
#: condinapt.1:241
msgid ""
"Simulation performs planning but no package installation.  It can update APT "
"list state and always exits 1, so its exit status is not a success indicator."
msgstr ""
"La simulation effectue la planification mais n'installe aucun paquet. Elle "
"peut mettre à jour l'état des listes APT et se termine toujours avec le code "
"1, ainsi son statut de sortie n'indique pas une réussite."

#. type: Plain text
#: condinapt.1:244
#, no-wrap
msgid "condinapt -l packages.list -c system.conf -m filters.map -s -v\n"
msgstr "condinapt -l packages.list -c system.conf -m filters.map -s -v\n"

#. type: SS
#: condinapt.1:245
#, no-wrap
msgid "Check Only"
msgstr "Vérification uniquement"

#. type: Plain text
#: condinapt.1:253
msgid ""
"Check-only evaluates filters and checks package names against the installed "
"package database.  It skips \\f[B]apt-get update\\f[R] and ignores version "
"and target-release requirements.  An alternative is satisfied when any "
"branch is installed.  If none is installed, the report and suggested command "
"may contain every failed branch rather than one availability-selected "
"alternative.\\fR"
msgstr ""
"Le mode vérification uniquement évalue les filtres et contrôle les noms de "
"paquets par rapport à la base de données des paquets installés. Il saute \\"
"\\f[B]apt-get update\\\\f[R] et ignore les exigences de version et de cible "
"de publication. Une alternative est considérée comme satisfaite dès qu'une "
"branche est installée. Si aucune n'est installée, le rapport et la commande "
"suggérée peuvent contenir toutes les branches échouées plutôt qu'une seule "
"alternative sélectionnée selon la disponibilité.\\\\fR"

#. type: Plain text
#: condinapt.1:256
#, no-wrap
msgid "condinapt -l packages.list -c system.conf -m filters.map -C\n"
msgstr "condinapt -l packages.list -c system.conf -m filters.map -C\n"

#. type: SH
#: condinapt.1:257
#, no-wrap
msgid "EXIT STATUS"
msgstr "STATUT DE SORTIE"

#. type: TP
#: condinapt.1:258
#, no-wrap
msgid "\\f[B]0\\fR"
msgstr "\\\\f[B]0\\\\fR"

#. type: Plain text
#: condinapt.1:262
msgid ""
"Installation completed, help was displayed, or check-only found no missing "
"packages."
msgstr ""
"Installation terminée, aide affichée ou aucune absence de paquet détectée en "
"mode vérification uniquement."

#. type: TP
#: condinapt.1:262
#, no-wrap
msgid "\\f[B]1\\fR"
msgstr "\\\\f[B]1\\\\fR"

#. type: Plain text
#: condinapt.1:266
msgid ""
"Invalid input, missing files, package or APT failure, missing packages in "
"check-only mode, or completion of simulation mode."
msgstr ""
"Entrée invalide, fichiers manquants, échec d'un paquet ou d'APT, paquets "
"manquants en mode vérification uniquement, ou fin du mode simulation."

#. type: Plain text
#: condinapt.1:272
msgid ""
"\\f[B]condinapt\\f[R] has no implicit configuration, mapping, or package-"
"list paths.  The package list and configuration must be supplied "
"explicitly.  The mapping and priority list are optional but are used only "
"when their paths are supplied.\\fR"
msgstr ""
"\\\\f[B]condinapt\\\\fR n'a pas de chemins implicites pour la configuration, "
"la correspondance ou la liste de paquets. La liste de paquets et la "
"configuration doivent être fournies explicitement. La correspondance et la "
"liste de priorités sont optionnelles mais ne sont utilisées que si leurs "
"chemins sont spécifiés.\\\\fR"

#. type: Plain text
#: condinapt.1:274
msgid "Install a filtered list:"
msgstr "Installer une liste filtrée :"

#. type: Plain text
#: condinapt.1:277
#, no-wrap
msgid "condinapt -l packages.list -c system.conf -m filters.map\n"
msgstr "condinapt -l packages.list -c system.conf -m filters.map\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: condinapt.1:280
msgid "Force an APT list refresh and install priority packages first:"
msgstr ""
"Forcer un rafraîchissement des listes APT et installer en priorité les "
"paquets listés dans la liste de priorités :"

#. type: Plain text
#: condinapt.1:284
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"condinapt -l packages.list -c system.conf -m filters.map \\[rs]\n"
"  -P priority.list -f\n"
msgstr ""
"condinapt -l packages.list -c system.conf -m filters.map \\\\[rs]\n"
"  -P priority.list -f\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: condinapt.1:288
msgid ""
"\\f[B]apt\\f[R](8), \\f[B]apt-get\\f[R](8), \\f[B]apt-cache\\f[R](8), "
"\\f[B]condinapt-minios\\f[R](7)\\fR"
msgstr ""
"\\f[B]apt\\f[R](8), \\f[B]apt-get\\f[R](8), \\f[B]apt-cache\\f[R](8), "
"\\f[B]condinapt-minios\\f[R](7)\\fR"
